1
00:01:38,070 --> 00:01:44,030
[Small Town Remedy]

2
00:01:44,210 --> 00:01:46,789
[Episode 29]

3
00:01:59,490 --> 00:02:05,590
[Tomb of Loving Father Liu Chunsheng
and Mother Li Zhongling]

4
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,510
Dad, Mom,

5
00:02:08,430 --> 00:02:10,229
Zhengguang and I came to see you.

6
00:02:11,430 --> 00:02:12,280
Mom, Dad.

7
00:02:15,750 --> 00:02:17,150
Why did you bring me here?

8
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:20,410
What do you think of this place?

9
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:24,329
What do you mean?

10
00:02:25,079 --> 00:02:25,870
Zhengguang.

11
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:28,620
I've thought about it for a long time.

12
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:29,870
When I get old,

13
00:02:30,430 --> 00:02:31,690
I'll come to this place

14
00:02:31,710 --> 00:02:33,040
and buy two tombstones,

15
00:02:34,520 --> 00:02:36,000
one for you and one for me.

16
00:02:38,280 --> 00:02:39,540
What's wrong with you?

17
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:40,820
Can't you talk nicely?

18
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:42,360
I'm in my twenties,

19
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:43,840
and you're in your thirties.

20
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:44,680
Are you in a bit of a hurry?

21
00:02:44,680 --> 00:02:45,430
So what?

22
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:47,220
No matter how young we are now,

23
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:48,000
we'll die sooner or later.

24
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:49,870
That's a long time from now.

25
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:51,520
Who knows where we'll be

26
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:52,650
when the time comes?

27
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:54,960
Where could we be?

28
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:56,840
Beijing,

29
00:02:57,840 --> 00:02:58,630
or Shenzhen?

30
00:02:59,079 --> 00:03:00,430
Or further abroad,

31
00:03:00,630 --> 00:03:01,430
like New York.

32
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:04,540
No matter where we are,

33
00:03:05,190 --> 00:03:06,630
I'll be buried here.

34
00:03:07,870 --> 00:03:09,930
Fallen leaves return to their roots.

35
00:03:10,150 --> 00:03:11,590
Our whole family is here.

36
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:13,840
This is our root.

37
00:03:14,910 --> 00:03:16,370
As long as our root is here,

38
00:03:16,470 --> 00:03:17,840
no matter what you want to do
along the way,

39
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:18,900
it doesn't matter.

40
00:03:19,280 --> 00:03:21,210
You can explore as much as you want.

41
00:03:23,310 --> 00:03:24,000
However...

42
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:24,750
Zhengguang.

43
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:26,800
Anyway, people

44
00:03:27,190 --> 00:03:28,450
will all die in the end.

45
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:29,520
Since we know

46
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:30,680
we will end up here,

47
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:33,370
we can live however we want.

48
00:03:34,630 --> 00:03:35,630
Zhengliang. I...

49
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:37,329
Why can't you figure it out?

50
00:03:37,430 --> 00:03:38,710
I agree with you.

51
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:41,170
I just have one request.

52
00:03:42,190 --> 00:03:43,190
When you buy them,

53
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:44,960
leave some space in between.

54
00:03:45,120 --> 00:03:46,579
Let's keep some distance,

55
00:03:46,960 --> 00:03:48,690
otherwise we'll easily argue.

56
00:03:51,750 --> 00:03:52,840
Are you serious?

57
00:04:02,150 --> 00:04:03,610
Say goodbye to Mom and Dad.

58
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:04,760
Let's go home.

59
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:09,480
We're leaving, Mom, Dad.

60
00:04:11,280 --> 00:04:12,150
What home?

61
00:04:12,190 --> 00:04:13,520
We don't have a home now.

62
00:04:13,590 --> 00:04:14,630
Didn't we sell the house?

63
00:04:14,630 --> 00:04:15,960
Housing prices in Fucheng are low.

64
00:04:15,960 --> 00:04:17,290
We can buy it back later.

65
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:19,190
You are quite something.

66
00:04:19,190 --> 00:04:19,920
You're really good at

67
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:21,430
making things sound so easy.

68
00:04:21,430 --> 00:04:22,560
Really impressive.

69
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:23,530
Warm up a little.

70
00:04:24,070 --> 00:04:24,560
Why?

71
00:04:25,750 --> 00:04:26,480
Get ready.

72
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:28,430
Let's see

73
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:30,930
who can run to the cemetery gate first.

74
00:04:31,190 --> 00:04:32,510
Are you 10?

75
00:04:32,510 --> 00:04:33,640
Three, two, one, go!

76
00:04:34,070 --> 00:04:35,070
The loser treats!

77
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,130
Why do I have to compete with you again?

78
00:04:38,630 --> 00:04:39,720
You jumped the gun!

79
00:04:40,040 --> 00:04:41,840
Liu Zhengguang, you're old now!

80
00:04:44,880 --> 00:04:52,040
[Fucheng City Taxi]

81
00:05:21,510 --> 00:05:23,560
It looks like you're physically strong,

82
00:05:23,560 --> 00:05:24,920
your arms and legs are in good shape,

83
00:05:24,920 --> 00:05:26,120
and your mind is clear.

84
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:28,320
Why don't you find something else to do?

85
00:05:29,360 --> 00:05:30,820
This place is so desolate.

86
00:05:30,870 --> 00:05:32,270
At night, the wind

87
00:05:33,920 --> 00:05:34,680
howls like crazy.

88
00:05:34,680 --> 00:05:38,720
[Patrolling. Please Wait a Moment]

89
00:05:34,830 --> 00:05:37,159
The elders say
it's full of yin energy here.

90
00:05:37,159 --> 00:05:38,070
Aren't you afraid of ghosts?

91
00:05:38,070 --> 00:05:38,830
I'm not.

92
00:05:39,950 --> 00:05:41,680
I'm afraid there are no ghosts.

93
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:43,810
Isn't it better if there are no ghosts?

94
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:44,720
Well,

95
00:05:44,720 --> 00:05:46,780
you want to see something scary here?

96
00:05:46,790 --> 00:05:54,330
[Patrolling. Please Wait a Moment]

97
00:05:47,310 --> 00:05:49,190
My wife passed away not long ago

98
00:05:49,630 --> 00:05:50,760
and was buried here.

99
00:05:51,190 --> 00:05:52,270
I've been thinking,

100
00:05:52,270 --> 00:05:54,630
maybe one day she'll come back to see me.

101
00:05:55,270 --> 00:05:57,000
They say this thing wards off evil,

102
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:59,600
but it can't stop people
from missing someone.

103
00:05:59,870 --> 00:06:01,200
It's cold here at night.

104
00:06:01,830 --> 00:06:03,030
You should wear more.

105
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:15,560
Chen.

106
00:06:18,120 --> 00:06:19,180
Comrade Changhai?

107
00:06:19,390 --> 00:06:20,270
Why are you here?

108
00:06:20,270 --> 00:06:22,200
Commissioner Chen, call me Uncle.

109
00:06:22,830 --> 00:06:23,310
Uncle Che,

110
00:06:23,310 --> 00:06:24,630
are you clear-headed

111
00:06:24,630 --> 00:06:25,750
or confused?

112
00:06:26,830 --> 00:06:27,960
Your Uncle Changhai

113
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:29,630
knows when to be confused

114
00:06:29,630 --> 00:06:30,680
and when to be

115
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:31,800
clear-headed.

116
00:06:31,830 --> 00:06:33,230
He knows what he's doing.

117
00:06:34,630 --> 00:06:35,690
What's the matter?

118
00:06:37,920 --> 00:06:38,750
Junnan,

119
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:41,950
life is...

120
00:06:41,950 --> 00:06:42,920
You're still young,

121
00:06:42,920 --> 00:06:44,310
so you may not feel the same way.

122
00:06:44,310 --> 00:06:45,720
Well, life is

123
00:06:45,720 --> 00:06:47,270
not so short,

124
00:06:47,270 --> 00:06:48,040
nor is it

125
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:49,510
so long.

126
00:06:49,950 --> 00:06:50,880
What I want to say

127
00:06:52,040 --> 00:06:53,570
is that you must cherish it.

128
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:55,360
Alright.

129
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:57,480
That's all I have to say.

130
00:06:58,070 --> 00:06:58,930
As for the rest,

131
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:02,240
you have to figure out for yourself.

132
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:05,680
I'll leave you alone.

133
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:15,460
[Little Pepper Stage]

134
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:21,070
This is your last time

135
00:07:21,070 --> 00:07:22,040
on stage, right?

136
00:07:23,750 --> 00:07:25,210
I want to sing a song I like.

137
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:27,920
That's good.

138
00:07:28,430 --> 00:07:29,510
In the future,

139
00:07:29,510 --> 00:07:30,950
I can brag to others,

140
00:07:31,120 --> 00:07:32,430
"My former partner

141
00:07:32,510 --> 00:07:33,920
has a PhD!"

142
00:07:36,390 --> 00:07:37,159
Who knows

143
00:07:37,159 --> 00:07:38,680
what will happen in Beijing?

144
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:39,750
You've been working so hard.

145
00:07:39,750 --> 00:07:41,010
Nothing will go wrong.

146
00:07:42,390 --> 00:07:43,850
I was just lucky this time.

147
00:07:44,190 --> 00:07:45,560
I know how things turned out.

148
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:46,600
I barely passed.

149
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:49,510
I just worked hard on my English and the interview.

150
00:07:49,510 --> 00:07:51,430
Fortunately, my former boss helped me

151
00:07:51,430 --> 00:07:52,240
and got me

152
00:07:52,240 --> 00:07:53,680
two strong letters of recommendation.

153
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:55,720
Otherwise,
I definitely wouldn't have made it.

154
00:07:55,720 --> 00:07:57,070
You're just being modest.

155
00:07:57,070 --> 00:07:58,750
I think you're really excellent.

156
00:07:58,750 --> 00:08:01,010
You'll definitely make it in the future.

157
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:02,390
Why?

158
00:08:02,560 --> 00:08:03,360
No reason.

159
00:08:04,310 --> 00:08:06,270
I'm just sincerely wishing you well.

160
00:08:06,270 --> 00:08:07,000
Who doesn't want

161
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:08,360
the doctors in their hometown

162
00:08:08,360 --> 00:08:09,420
to be more awesome?

163
00:08:09,750 --> 00:08:11,070
But what if I don't come back

164
00:08:11,070 --> 00:08:12,400
after I become awesome?

165
00:08:14,360 --> 00:08:15,360
That's also good.

166
00:08:15,390 --> 00:08:16,430
People always aim
for bigger and better things.

167
00:08:16,430 --> 00:08:17,240
Right, Sis?

168
00:08:18,870 --> 00:08:20,000
I'm just kidding.

169
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:21,390
How could I not come back?

170
00:08:21,390 --> 00:08:22,560
My dad is here.

171
00:08:22,560 --> 00:08:23,950
If I leave, who will take care of him?

172
00:08:23,950 --> 00:08:25,720
You can take him with you.

173
00:08:27,270 --> 00:08:28,360
Sis, why

174
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:29,630
do you think people

175
00:08:29,630 --> 00:08:31,000
like going to the South?

176
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:32,840
Is it just to make money?

177
00:08:32,870 --> 00:08:36,200
But although you make more money there,
you also spend more.

178
00:08:36,510 --> 00:08:37,789
In my opinion,

179
00:08:39,320 --> 00:08:40,630
it's because it's too cold here.

180
00:08:40,630 --> 00:08:42,030
Anyone with the means

181
00:08:42,030 --> 00:08:42,669
wants to

182
00:08:42,669 --> 00:08:44,000
go somewhere warm.

183
00:08:44,600 --> 00:08:46,240
Just look at other countries.

184
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:47,360
It's not just us.

185
00:08:47,870 --> 00:08:49,240
Northerners all over the world

186
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:50,500
want to go to the South.

187
00:08:52,150 --> 00:08:53,320
It's that simple?

188
00:08:53,360 --> 00:08:54,360
It's that simple.

189
00:09:02,870 --> 00:09:03,960
As the saying goes,

190
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:05,150
"I'd rather skip a meal

191
00:09:05,150 --> 00:09:06,600
than miss a sing-and-dance duet."

192
00:09:06,600 --> 00:09:07,390
Guys,

193
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:08,910
did you like Guo and Jia's

194
00:09:08,910 --> 00:09:10,150
performance?

195
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:11,240
Yes!

196
00:09:10,450 --> 00:09:14,250
[Little Pepper Stage]

197
00:09:12,080 --> 00:09:13,670
Now, let's give

198
00:09:13,670 --> 00:09:15,150
a warm round of applause

199
00:09:15,150 --> 00:09:16,750
to Big Pomegranate,

200
00:09:16,750 --> 00:09:18,150
who will perform

201
00:09:18,150 --> 00:09:20,360
"Train to Spring."

202
00:09:20,440 --> 00:09:22,370
Please welcome her with applause!

203
00:09:22,620 --> 00:09:28,250
[Train To Spring, Big Pomegranates]

204
00:09:26,150 --> 00:09:27,150
Are you ready?

205
00:09:45,110 --> 00:09:48,080
I ran across the snowy sky in the north

206
00:09:48,730 --> 00:09:52,440
I've been to the rainy night in the south

207
00:09:53,500 --> 00:09:55,390
Train goes to that spring

208
00:09:55,630 --> 00:09:57,720
Every dream will come true

209
00:09:58,300 --> 00:10:00,010
Storms and storms

210
00:10:00,370 --> 00:10:02,310
The flowers will bloom at the end

211
00:10:02,610 --> 00:10:04,360
Let's go back to the mountain

212
00:10:04,850 --> 00:10:06,730
We'll go through snow

213
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:09,060
The people I miss will meet

214
00:10:09,360 --> 00:10:11,140
They said don't be afraid

215
00:10:11,690 --> 00:10:14,610
Look forward to tomorrow

216
00:10:17,310 --> 00:10:21,830
[Little Pepper Stage]

217
00:10:33,390 --> 00:10:34,270
Bravo!

218
00:10:37,200 --> 00:10:37,750
Bravo!

219
00:11:03,360 --> 00:11:04,080
You look kind of lonely

220
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:05,120
sitting here.

221
00:11:09,120 --> 00:11:09,670
Here.

222
00:11:10,120 --> 00:11:13,320
You're sweating like crazy.
It'll help you recover a bit.

223
00:11:14,150 --> 00:11:15,120
You're a good friend.

224
00:11:15,120 --> 00:11:15,600
You have some.

225
00:11:15,600 --> 00:11:16,120
I won't.

226
00:11:18,600 --> 00:11:19,660
Let me see your eye.

227
00:11:23,750 --> 00:11:24,440
Are you okay?

228
00:11:24,440 --> 00:11:25,150
I'm fine.

229
00:11:25,630 --> 00:11:26,480
It's nothing.

230
00:11:27,790 --> 00:11:29,080
This punch was totally worth it.

231
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:30,670
That guy felt bad

232
00:11:30,870 --> 00:11:32,270
and wrote us a 100-word

233
00:11:32,270 --> 00:11:33,330
five-star review.

234
00:11:33,390 --> 00:11:34,270
Don't you think it was worth it?

235
00:11:34,270 --> 00:11:34,910
Yes.

236
00:11:42,790 --> 00:11:44,360
I need to tell you something.

237
00:11:44,360 --> 00:11:46,630
Just say it. No need to announce it.

238
00:11:46,630 --> 00:11:47,390
Just say it.

239
00:11:50,120 --> 00:11:51,600
I'm planning to go to Beijing

240
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:53,400
to start a business with Junnan.

241
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:04,000
That's great.

242
00:12:05,390 --> 00:12:06,520
Junnan is a good guy.

243
00:12:07,440 --> 00:12:08,500
He's kind-hearted

244
00:12:08,960 --> 00:12:09,840
and loyal.

245
00:12:09,910 --> 00:12:11,440
He gets along well with you.

246
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:14,340
What about you?

247
00:12:14,910 --> 00:12:17,110
I definitely get along better with you.

248
00:12:18,030 --> 00:12:19,790
Aren't we soulmates?

249
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:22,100
Are you stupid?

250
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:24,450
Is that what I'm talking about?

251
00:12:25,150 --> 00:12:26,270
I got it.

252
00:12:26,750 --> 00:12:27,750
Just kidding.

253
00:12:27,750 --> 00:12:29,550
You have no sense of humor.

254
00:12:30,910 --> 00:12:31,750
Look,

255
00:12:31,840 --> 00:12:32,750
our business

256
00:12:32,750 --> 00:12:33,870
is stable now.

257
00:12:34,390 --> 00:12:36,450
I'm planning to hire two more actors,

258
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:38,440
make the horror experience more intense,

259
00:12:38,440 --> 00:12:39,500
and make it bigger.

260
00:12:40,670 --> 00:12:41,870
You are the chairman.

261
00:12:41,870 --> 00:12:43,470
Just wait for the dividends.

262
00:12:43,670 --> 00:12:44,480
Don't interfere

263
00:12:44,480 --> 00:12:46,120
with my business as the general manager.

264
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:47,720
Go do whatever you need to do.

265
00:12:51,080 --> 00:12:51,910
This time,

266
00:12:53,030 --> 00:12:53,910
if I don't make a name for myself,

267
00:12:53,910 --> 00:12:54,960
I won't come back.

268
00:12:59,440 --> 00:13:01,040
Get along well with Gong Xue.

269
00:13:03,910 --> 00:13:04,720
I'm leaving.

270
00:13:08,870 --> 00:13:10,870
Remember to come back if you do well.

271
00:13:11,550 --> 00:13:13,550
If you don't, come back quickly too.

272
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:16,320
Don't forget,

273
00:13:17,150 --> 00:13:19,080
someone is waiting for you at home.

274
00:13:29,480 --> 00:13:31,690
[1314 Funeral Services]

275
00:13:33,150 --> 00:13:35,200
Besides the router, is there anything else

276
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:36,320
your dad needs?

277
00:13:38,840 --> 00:13:39,630
No.

278
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,240
Let me tell you a joke.

279
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:50,030
You can tell jokes?

280
00:13:50,960 --> 00:13:51,960
Of course I can.

281
00:13:52,510 --> 00:13:53,960
When I was in Shenzhen,

282
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:55,610
I even did stand-up comedy.

283
00:13:55,910 --> 00:13:57,370
You couldn't tell, right?

284
00:13:59,360 --> 00:14:00,360
Did anyone laugh?

285
00:14:00,910 --> 00:14:02,640
No one in the audience laughed,

286
00:14:02,720 --> 00:14:05,320
but the actors backstage
went crazy laughing.

287
00:14:06,360 --> 00:14:07,560
That's pretty funny.

288
00:14:07,610 --> 00:14:10,490
[Tianshan Road]

289
00:14:11,440 --> 00:14:12,390
4 scales in total.

290
00:14:12,390 --> 00:14:13,200
15 catties, 15 catties.

291
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:13,910
Four scales added together,

292
00:14:13,910 --> 00:14:15,550
82.7 catties.

293
00:14:14,040 --> 00:14:15,620
[Cabbage on Sale]

294
00:14:15,910 --> 00:14:17,270
Four scales, 82.7 catties.

295
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:17,540
[Cabbage on Sale]

296
00:14:19,080 --> 00:14:20,030
82.7, charge for 82.

297
00:14:20,030 --> 00:14:20,750
Is it them?

298
00:14:20,750 --> 00:14:21,510
Charge for 82.

299
00:14:21,510 --> 00:14:22,870
82 catties, 82 catties.

300
00:14:22,960 --> 00:14:23,480
Yes.

301
00:14:25,510 --> 00:14:27,000
This is too little.

302
00:14:27,320 --> 00:14:28,510
How can you round off so much?

303
00:14:28,510 --> 00:14:30,440
You can't round off that much, sir!

304
00:14:31,600 --> 00:14:33,730
Zhang Jiao should be fully recovered.

305
00:14:36,320 --> 00:14:38,380
It looks that way. She looks fine now.

306
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:40,750
Let's go say hi.

307
00:14:42,910 --> 00:14:43,750
Forget it.

308
00:14:44,150 --> 00:14:45,630
As long as they are doing well now,

309
00:14:45,630 --> 00:14:46,490
that's enough.

310
00:14:46,630 --> 00:14:47,890
Let's not bother them.

311
00:14:49,750 --> 00:14:50,630
Alright.

312
00:14:59,270 --> 00:15:00,200
It's delicious!

313
00:15:22,440 --> 00:15:23,840
Wait for me here for a bit.

314
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:24,630
Okay.

315
00:15:24,630 --> 00:15:26,270
Call me if you need anything.

316
00:15:26,870 --> 00:15:27,840
Don't worry.

317
00:15:28,270 --> 00:15:30,200
Haven't you taught me everything?

318
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:49,640
[Anti-Riot Equipment Cabinet]

319
00:15:49,670 --> 00:15:50,870
Where's Zhengliang?

320
00:15:51,080 --> 00:15:52,880
I told him to wait for me outside.

321
00:15:55,790 --> 00:15:57,120
Since my mom left,

322
00:15:57,720 --> 00:15:58,550
it's been a long time

323
00:15:58,550 --> 00:16:00,120
since we talked,

324
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:00,840
hasn't it?

325
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:03,000
Yes.

326
00:16:04,550 --> 00:16:06,150
But let me tell you, daughter,

327
00:16:06,150 --> 00:16:07,670
I'm doing fine now.

328
00:16:10,240 --> 00:16:11,390
I'm staying here

329
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:13,120
because I feel

330
00:16:14,030 --> 00:16:15,840
that the time your mom and I

331
00:16:16,070 --> 00:16:17,470
had together in this life

332
00:16:17,870 --> 00:16:18,790
was too short.

333
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:20,960
If she wasn't in,

334
00:16:21,240 --> 00:16:21,960
I was in.

335
00:16:21,960 --> 00:16:22,510
If I wasn't in,

336
00:16:22,510 --> 00:16:23,390
she was in.

337
00:16:24,600 --> 00:16:26,730
We didn't spend enough time together.

338
00:16:26,960 --> 00:16:28,200
I was thinking,

339
00:16:28,910 --> 00:16:30,440
if I work here,

340
00:16:31,720 --> 00:16:33,630
I can be closer to her.

341
00:16:38,960 --> 00:16:39,750
Dad.

342
00:16:41,480 --> 00:16:42,840
I know you feel bad.

343
00:16:45,550 --> 00:16:46,480
I'm not against you

344
00:16:46,480 --> 00:16:47,510
working here.

345
00:16:48,440 --> 00:16:49,970
But we have to move forward.

346
00:16:53,670 --> 00:16:54,790
I'm sure Mom would

347
00:16:54,790 --> 00:16:55,960
want you to do the same.

348
00:16:55,960 --> 00:16:57,510
We can't just stop here.

349
00:16:58,390 --> 00:16:59,960
Didn't you tell me

350
00:17:00,480 --> 00:17:02,340
that this is what our family does?

351
00:17:15,589 --> 00:17:16,510
Before,

352
00:17:16,510 --> 00:17:18,109
I didn't like hazelnuts.

353
00:17:19,480 --> 00:17:20,609
Your mom loved them.

354
00:17:21,200 --> 00:17:23,060
But she didn't like to shell them.

355
00:17:24,109 --> 00:17:25,200
So she made me do it.

356
00:17:25,200 --> 00:17:27,260
If I said no, she'd give me a hard time.

357
00:17:29,070 --> 00:17:31,830
So I just... I just did it for her.

358
00:17:32,920 --> 00:17:33,680
Yeah...

359
00:17:35,030 --> 00:17:35,880
I would...

360
00:17:36,440 --> 00:17:37,920
I'd shell one for her,

361
00:17:38,830 --> 00:17:39,920
and eat one myself.

362
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:41,550
Shell one for her,

363
00:17:42,510 --> 00:17:43,680
and eat one myself.

364
00:17:45,750 --> 00:17:47,010
After doing it so much,

365
00:17:48,200 --> 00:17:49,750
I started to like them too.

366
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:53,110
Well...

367
00:17:58,550 --> 00:18:00,010
I shelled too many of them.

368
00:18:00,440 --> 00:18:01,880
Take them with you later.

369
00:18:03,350 --> 00:18:04,410
You and Zhengliang

370
00:18:04,960 --> 00:18:06,220
can eat them together.

371
00:18:10,790 --> 00:18:11,510
Dad.

372
00:18:12,240 --> 00:18:14,400
I know. You're right.

373
00:18:15,110 --> 00:18:16,440
We should move forward.

374
00:18:17,830 --> 00:18:18,680
You're young.

375
00:18:19,270 --> 00:18:20,670
You have to move forward.

376
00:18:22,510 --> 00:18:26,200
You are the continuation

377
00:18:27,550 --> 00:18:29,440
of your mom and me.

378
00:18:30,590 --> 00:18:31,990
You have to move forward.

379
00:18:32,310 --> 00:18:33,640
I'm not going anywhere.

380
00:18:33,830 --> 00:18:35,230
I'm stopping right here.

381
00:18:39,920 --> 00:18:40,680
It's fine.

382
00:19:00,660 --> 00:19:06,050
[1314 Funeral Services]

383
00:19:08,220 --> 00:19:13,650
[1314 Funeral Services]

384
00:19:28,310 --> 00:19:29,170
What are these?

385
00:19:36,310 --> 00:19:37,160
Memories.

386
00:19:37,510 --> 00:19:38,510
Memories?

387
00:19:44,160 --> 00:19:45,790
Aren't these just hazelnuts?

388
00:19:45,790 --> 00:19:46,720
Do you like them?

389
00:19:50,510 --> 00:19:51,510
Not really.

390
00:19:53,550 --> 00:19:54,350
Eat more.

391
00:19:55,680 --> 00:19:57,010
Maybe you'll like them.

392
00:20:21,920 --> 00:20:22,750
Let's go.

393
00:20:26,320 --> 00:20:29,470
♪ A soul that came to earth
amid the cries ♪

394
00:20:29,920 --> 00:20:33,020
♪ Welcome to this city of haste ♪

395
00:20:33,530 --> 00:20:35,820
♪ Grow taller, quick as you can ♪

396
00:20:36,190 --> 00:20:38,500
♪ Learn how to find your footing ♪

397
00:20:40,660 --> 00:20:43,990
♪ A soul who hid
among the lanes and alleys ♪

398
00:20:44,490 --> 00:20:47,690
♪ A single turn, and the lamp
at the door grows distant ♪

399
00:20:46,790 --> 00:20:47,590
Amy

400
00:20:48,090 --> 00:20:50,480
♪ The ticket bears no way back ♪

401
00:20:50,400 --> 00:20:53,000
Come on. Let me help you clean up today.

402
00:20:50,770 --> 00:20:53,160
♪ How like life it is ♪

403
00:20:55,130 --> 00:21:02,100
[Mother, Mi Xiaoxia]

404
00:20:55,420 --> 00:20:57,920
♪ May every road you take be safe ♪

405
00:20:57,200 --> 00:20:58,200
It's clean

406
00:20:58,110 --> 00:21:02,220
♪ May the scenery stay simple
and carry you past regret ♪

407
00:21:02,730 --> 00:21:05,840
♪ Love deeply whatever comes to meet you ♪

408
00:21:03,430 --> 00:21:06,990
[In Memory]

409
00:21:06,350 --> 00:21:09,480
♪ And let those who leave be buried
under snow on the hills ♪

410
00:21:10,040 --> 00:21:12,530
♪ May you come home covered in dust ♪

411
00:21:12,790 --> 00:21:16,770
♪ Held by what you love
as you roam the world and return ♪

412
00:21:15,870 --> 00:21:19,700
[Mother, Mi Xiaoxia]

413
00:21:18,120 --> 00:21:22,570
♪ Saying the flowers
by the door are truly beautiful ♪

414
00:21:27,680 --> 00:21:29,000
I'm getting you a new one.

415
00:21:28,330 --> 00:21:31,540
♪ You'll pass through the seasons,
through dawn and dusk ♪

416
00:21:31,910 --> 00:21:35,190
♪ Hearing someone call your name,
again and again ♪

417
00:21:35,240 --> 00:21:36,160
One day

418
00:21:35,480 --> 00:21:37,960
♪ It hurts to say goodbye ♪

419
00:21:38,260 --> 00:21:40,720
♪ If you can't recover, just wait ♪

420
00:21:39,590 --> 00:21:40,790
There are many kids here.

421
00:21:40,790 --> 00:21:42,270
What if they like it?

422
00:21:42,950 --> 00:21:46,000
♪ It will bear witness
to the life you bravely lived ♪

423
00:21:44,270 --> 00:21:45,680
We are professionals.

424
00:21:46,400 --> 00:21:47,400
We can't let amateurs

425
00:21:46,570 --> 00:21:49,860
♪ To the beautiful souls you've loved ♪

426
00:21:47,400 --> 00:21:48,830
take our business.

427
00:21:49,590 --> 00:21:50,310
Right?

428
00:21:50,220 --> 00:21:52,340
♪ To the address you call home ♪

429
00:21:52,830 --> 00:21:57,720
♪ We come to each other ♪

430
00:21:58,960 --> 00:22:01,030
You drive really well.

431
00:22:01,480 --> 00:22:02,720
Better than my dad

432
00:22:02,720 --> 00:22:03,850
and Rainbow Pillar.

433
00:22:05,110 --> 00:22:07,310
It's okay. I'm driving steadily today.

434
00:22:12,400 --> 00:22:14,660
I'm going to take the Subject 2 test soon.

435
00:22:16,550 --> 00:22:18,280
What's wrong? Are you nervous?

436
00:22:18,880 --> 00:22:20,440
It's fine. It's easy.

437
00:22:21,270 --> 00:22:22,920
If you fail, just take it again.

438
00:22:22,920 --> 00:22:24,070
I took it twice.

439
00:22:25,960 --> 00:22:27,200
You took it twice?

440
00:22:28,110 --> 00:22:29,840
I was taking the Subject 3 test.

441
00:22:30,590 --> 00:22:31,880
Isn't it two people in one car,

442
00:22:31,880 --> 00:22:32,830
taking turns?

443
00:22:33,400 --> 00:22:34,790
I felt that my examiner

444
00:22:34,790 --> 00:22:35,480
was very disrespectful to the person

445
00:22:35,480 --> 00:22:37,010
who took the test before me.

446
00:22:37,070 --> 00:22:38,270
So I tried to reason with him,

447
00:22:38,270 --> 00:22:39,400
and we ended up arguing.

448
00:22:39,400 --> 00:22:40,160
In the end, the examiner

449
00:22:40,160 --> 00:22:41,720
kicked me out of the car before I even got

450
00:22:41,720 --> 00:22:43,160
to touch the steering wheel.

451
00:22:43,160 --> 00:22:44,640
That was a pity.

452
00:22:46,160 --> 00:22:47,030
Why didn't you hold it in?

453
00:22:47,030 --> 00:22:48,480
You could have... well...

454
00:22:48,480 --> 00:22:50,480
argued with him after the test.

455
00:22:50,750 --> 00:22:51,790
Come on.

456
00:22:51,790 --> 00:22:52,790
Could you hold it in if you were me?

457
00:22:52,790 --> 00:22:54,030
How could I?

458
00:22:54,920 --> 00:22:55,720
I don't put up

459
00:22:55,720 --> 00:22:57,380
with being treated unfairly.

460
00:22:58,110 --> 00:23:00,200
I must be happy every day.

461
00:23:00,350 --> 00:23:01,880
What if someone disagrees?

462
00:23:02,480 --> 00:23:03,610
Disagree with what?

463
00:23:05,400 --> 00:23:07,590
Disagree with you being happy every day.

464
00:23:07,590 --> 00:23:08,720
Who would disagree?

465
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:09,480
I don't know.

466
00:23:09,590 --> 00:23:11,400
Just assuming there is such a person.

467
00:23:11,400 --> 00:23:12,750
I'd slap him in the face.

468
00:23:13,830 --> 00:23:14,830
Disagree?

469
00:23:15,030 --> 00:23:17,560
I don't need anyone's permission
to be happy.

470
00:23:17,920 --> 00:23:19,000
What if it's just

471
00:23:19,270 --> 00:23:21,110
that you think you don't need it?

472
00:23:24,590 --> 00:23:25,400
What's wrong?

473
00:23:25,550 --> 00:23:26,720
Do you disagree with it?

474
00:23:26,720 --> 00:23:27,920
Of course not.

475
00:23:27,920 --> 00:23:29,450
If you're happy, I'm happy.

476
00:23:41,400 --> 00:23:42,160
What are you doing?

477
00:23:42,160 --> 00:23:43,090
Aren't you cold?

478
00:23:48,920 --> 00:23:49,960
Speed up!

479
00:23:56,700 --> 00:24:00,660
[For Dramatic Purposes Only.
Do Not Imitate.]

480
00:23:59,160 --> 00:24:00,480
I feel it.

481
00:24:04,070 --> 00:24:05,480
My mom agrees too!

482
00:24:07,480 --> 00:24:09,720
She wants me to be happy every day.

483
00:24:11,350 --> 00:24:12,920
I must be happy!

484
00:24:30,480 --> 00:24:32,240
This place is so badass.

485
00:24:33,270 --> 00:24:34,350
What is this?

486
00:24:34,720 --> 00:24:36,050
"Eat skewers with gusto

487
00:24:37,030 --> 00:24:38,830
and drink to your heart's content."

488
00:24:38,830 --> 00:24:39,560
Not bad, huh?

489
00:24:39,960 --> 00:24:41,490
How did you find this place?

490
00:24:42,480 --> 00:24:43,750
Just tell me if it's good.

491
00:24:43,750 --> 00:24:44,950
Who did you come with?

492
00:24:46,480 --> 00:24:47,400
Chen Junnan.

493
00:24:48,790 --> 00:24:49,920
I was wondering.

494
00:24:50,160 --> 00:24:51,510
I thought you only knew how to call a cab,

495
00:24:51,510 --> 00:24:52,200
but you can also find places.

496
00:24:52,200 --> 00:24:53,920
Welcome to The Old Captain Restaurant.

497
00:24:53,920 --> 00:24:55,750
We have a lucky draw tonight.

498
00:24:55,750 --> 00:24:57,640
The first prize is a free meal.

499
00:24:58,310 --> 00:24:59,350
Let's try our luck.

500
00:24:59,350 --> 00:25:00,110
You draw.

501
00:25:00,240 --> 00:25:01,110
I draw?

502
00:25:02,240 --> 00:25:03,030
Mix them up.

503
00:25:03,240 --> 00:25:03,960
Draw one.

504
00:25:06,960 --> 00:25:07,550
This one.

505
00:25:09,550 --> 00:25:10,510
And this one.

506
00:25:14,270 --> 00:25:15,480
Congratulations!

507
00:25:16,070 --> 00:25:17,110
Thank you!

508
00:25:18,480 --> 00:25:20,400
What kind of luck was that?

509
00:25:20,960 --> 00:25:22,360
It was also my first time.

510
00:25:22,400 --> 00:25:23,000
Really?

511
00:25:23,000 --> 00:25:24,330
Never done this before.

512
00:25:25,070 --> 00:25:25,870
It's too cold.

513
00:25:27,650 --> 00:25:31,230
[The Old Captain Restaurant]

514
00:25:27,720 --> 00:25:29,120
You just have to be happy.

515
00:25:29,400 --> 00:25:30,960
Happiness brings good luck.

516
00:25:30,960 --> 00:25:31,550
Right.

517
00:25:32,830 --> 00:25:33,510
You're here.

518
00:25:33,510 --> 00:25:35,960
Let me see who's so lucky!

519
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:36,720
I am!

520
00:25:37,270 --> 00:25:38,240
I was amazing.

521
00:25:38,240 --> 00:25:39,270
It was my first time.

522
00:25:39,270 --> 00:25:39,930
So awesome.

523
00:25:40,510 --> 00:25:41,910
Your luck is incredible.

524
00:25:42,350 --> 00:25:43,440
A free meal.

525
00:25:43,590 --> 00:25:44,590
I really...

526
00:25:45,640 --> 00:25:46,310
Wait.

527
00:25:46,310 --> 00:25:47,400
How did they know?

528
00:25:47,480 --> 00:25:48,350
Well, here's the thing.

529
00:25:48,350 --> 00:25:49,350
I told them no one else could pay.

530
00:25:49,350 --> 00:25:50,030
I'm paying today.

531
00:25:50,030 --> 00:25:50,830
Then I told the staff

532
00:25:50,830 --> 00:25:52,750
to say we won a free meal.

533
00:25:53,350 --> 00:25:53,720
Well...

534
00:25:53,720 --> 00:25:55,030
This luck.

535
00:25:55,680 --> 00:25:57,070
Your luck brings wealth.

536
00:25:57,070 --> 00:25:57,640
Come on.

537
00:25:57,640 --> 00:25:58,680
Mingming, you drink this.

538
00:25:58,680 --> 00:26:00,030
This is... What's the word again?

539
00:26:00,030 --> 00:26:00,880
Zero sugar.

540
00:26:01,110 --> 00:26:02,510
Really?
No gain. No gain.

541
00:26:02,640 --> 00:26:03,640
Thank you, Huang.

542
00:26:03,680 --> 00:26:04,830
Let's have a drink
before we start grilling.

543
00:26:04,830 --> 00:26:05,480
Come on.

544
00:26:05,480 --> 00:26:06,640
Are you really doing this?

545
00:26:06,640 --> 00:26:07,270
Come on.

546
00:26:07,270 --> 00:26:07,750
Let's have a drink first.

547
00:26:07,750 --> 00:26:08,950
Have a drink. Come on.

548
00:26:09,640 --> 00:26:10,270
What should we do?

549
00:26:10,270 --> 00:26:10,830
It's fine.

550
00:26:10,830 --> 00:26:11,750
It's going to boil.

551
00:26:11,750 --> 00:26:12,440
It's going to boil.

552
00:26:12,440 --> 00:26:13,640
Flourishing.

553
00:26:14,880 --> 00:26:15,880
The vibe is perfect.

554
00:26:15,880 --> 00:26:16,880
Come on. Drink up.

555
00:26:18,590 --> 00:26:19,350
Let's grill.

556
00:26:19,480 --> 00:26:20,640
Grill the meat, come on.

557
00:26:20,640 --> 00:26:21,590
Come on, let's grill.

558
00:26:21,590 --> 00:26:22,590
It's sizzling.

559
00:26:24,440 --> 00:26:24,920
Well, I'll...

560
00:26:24,920 --> 00:26:26,120
I'll propose a toast.

561
00:26:28,590 --> 00:26:29,450
What did he say?

562
00:26:29,830 --> 00:26:31,110
I didn't hear it clearly either.

563
00:26:31,110 --> 00:26:32,710
He said he'd propose a toast.

564
00:26:32,880 --> 00:26:33,350
What?

565
00:26:34,160 --> 00:26:34,830
Zhengliang,

566
00:26:34,830 --> 00:26:36,640
you shouldn't have such bad habits.

567
00:26:36,640 --> 00:26:37,830
He was "polluted" by us.

568
00:26:37,830 --> 00:26:38,890
He got influenced.

569
00:26:39,440 --> 00:26:40,240
Wait a minute.

570
00:26:41,200 --> 00:26:43,000
Why is your wine steaming?

571
00:26:43,750 --> 00:26:45,400
Don't ask for too much.

572
00:26:45,640 --> 00:26:46,840
What more do you want?

573
00:26:46,880 --> 00:26:48,240
Be nicer to your brother.

574
00:26:48,240 --> 00:26:49,200
Are you the only one with a mouth?

575
00:26:49,200 --> 00:26:50,310
Alright, alright.

576
00:26:50,480 --> 00:26:52,240
Why so serious?

577
00:26:52,480 --> 00:26:54,550
You've... made some progress.

578
00:26:55,070 --> 00:26:57,270
You'll drink this steaming wine later.

579
00:26:57,880 --> 00:26:59,070
I'll drink his wine for him.

580
00:26:59,070 --> 00:26:59,750
